WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.020
I grew strong because of you!

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.680
I never forgot my smile...

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.040
Respond to me, Yuya! In front of everyone!

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.290
And come home with me. To our home.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.460
Now, it's the last turn, Yuya!

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.180
If you get scared and cringe, 
you can't do anything.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.740
If you want to win, then have courage...

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.380
...and step forward!

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.940
My... turn!

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.440
I activate Quick-Play Spell Smile Universe!

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.800
I Special Summon as many monsters as I can

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.160
from my Extra Deck, with effects negated!

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.670
The Supreme King Dragons are back.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.410
Can it be... He isn't Yuya?

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.280
Pendulum Monsters are invincible.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.210
No matter how many times they're 
destroyed, they'll come back to life.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.250
I won't let you! I'll put an end to what I started!

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.220
Wh-What are you doing? Stop it!

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.030
I've made up my mind.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.980
I won't be a devil anymore!

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.960
Now! Do it, Layra!

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:25.130
The effect of En Flowers

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.480
negates the effect of all monsters 
on the field and destroys them.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.640
And for each monster that's 
sent to the graveyard,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.760
I deal 600 damage to their controller!

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.970
Damn you...

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.610
I... will...

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.820
The world is trying to split into four again!

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:53.690
Z-ARC wants to separate the 
dimensions and repeat it all—

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.230
I won't let it happen again!

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.660
I'll seal Z-ARC myself!

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.010
Layra?

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.980
Layra!

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:20.420
Implementing mass into Solid Vision 
has created Action Duels.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.020
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.150
the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:07.030
The Junior Youth Championship

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.600
I overslept!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.640
What's the big hurry?

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.110
Today's Sunday. You don't 
have school, do you?

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.990
I have a duel at You Show School...

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.580
Our principal's passionate teachings!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.520
You're spitting food everywhere.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.680
Eat or talk, choose one.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.630
I'm off!

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.300
Sliding in safe—

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.590
That hurt! What are you doing?

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.190
Safe, my eye!

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.010
You're three minutes late!

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.350
Come on... Three minutes isn't a big deal.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:15.890
No, no!

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.360
The principal's passionate teachings 
have already begun!

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.890
What's that thing, anyway?

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.620
Oh, this?

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.720
Well it's, you know, the usual...

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.870
Huh?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.340
Why do I have this here?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.660
Wow, Yuya!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.580
Those boots are so cool!

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.070
They are, aren't they?

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.050
They give me shivers!

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.160
Where did you buy them?

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.160
I didn't buy them. They were a gift.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.200
From who?

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.330
Well...

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.130
Huh?

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:53.420
You forgot who gave them 
to you? That's so rude!

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.570
Yeah!

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:59.600
Hey! That's enough talking out of you all!

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.520
It's time to get dueling!

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.320
Look lively already!

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.080
Yes, sir!

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.390
Okay!

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.020
Let's change things up with 
a one-on-three duel!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.900
I'll take you all on at once, 
so give me a good fight, okay?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.130
Looking good, Yuya!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.170
You Show school's greatest duelist,

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:28.930
the entertainer of his age, and your father, 
is out traveling the world,

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.100
teaching others about entertainment duels!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:36.210
You need to become a great pro duelist, 
just like him, as soon as possible!

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:41.960
Field Spell Plain Plain, activate!

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.560
The duelists meet at the battlefield!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.530
Along with their monsters, they'll kick 
the ground and fly through the sky

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.490
to move around the field!

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:59.460
Witness dueling's greatest evolution.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.180
Action...

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:02.780
Duel!

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.280
I'll go first!

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.700
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 1 Stargazer Magician

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:13.340
and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician from my hand!

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.590
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.560
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.530
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.290
Pendulum Summon!

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.230
Come out, my monsters...

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.740
Performapal Sword Fish!

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.210
Performapal Whip Snake!

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:45.310
And the rare dragon with two 
different-colored eyes,

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.580
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:49.550
I end my turn.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.520
My turn! Draw!

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.720
I set the Pendulum Scale 
with Scale 1 Deskbot 008

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:01.530
and Scale 10 Deskbot 007!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.930
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 10 simultaneously.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.070
Pendulum Summon!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.360
Deskbot 005!

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.110
And Deskbot 006!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:21.080
The Pendulum Dimension?

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:22.950
Yes.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.170
This world, once the Standard Dimension,

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:29.020
has been reborn as the Pendulum Dimension.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:34.230
Right now, anyone can Pendulum Summon, 
as if it were only natural.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:38.200
Yes... Ever since that day.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.670
And that child...

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.180
I have already taken measures.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:47.050
Do not worry, Mother.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.020
My turn!

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.380
Okay, here we go, Yuya.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.530
What's this?

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.460
What?!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.460
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:19.400
Ow...

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.010
Yuya! Emergency!

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.480
Look... Look at this, Yuya!

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:28.180
Is this from LDS?

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.040
That's right. It's an invitation to the 
Junior Youth Championship.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.560
If you win there, you can advance to Youth.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.870
A chance to become a pro duelist 
has fallen right in your lap!

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.720
That's so cool, Yuya!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.200
Gives me shivers!

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.900
What are you doing, Yuya?

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.430
Go on, get to LDS right now!

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.220
Yeah! I'm off!

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:56.110
All right. That concludes your registration.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.840
Good luck, Yuya Sakaki.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.220
S-Sure... Thanks a bunch.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.310
Yuya!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.080
I knew you'd get one, too.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.320
An invitation to the Junior 
Youth Championship.

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:10.890
Gongenzaka!

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:13.560
Well, well... I see you're both here.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.960
Sawatari!

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.680
Unbelievable. You got an invitation, too?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.080
What do you mean by "unbelievable"?!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.080
Of course I got one.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.720
My father is expected to be the next mayor,

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:29.070
and I'm a born leader, 
with top grades at LDS.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:32.590
The super, ultra, hyper-strong duelist...

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:33.600
Reiji Akaba!

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.690
Yes, Reiji Akaba.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.350
Wait, what?!

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.000
I see you're all here.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:45.020
I'd like you three to first duel at this 
Junior Youth Championship.

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.630
A battle royal through Maiami City.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.300
Battle royal?

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.740
Everyone, sorry for the wait!

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:04.240
We will now commence the 
Junior Youth Championship!

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.200
Now, let me introduce the four 
participating challengers!

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.990
Wait, only four?

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.630
It's true.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:20.430
Well then, let me introduce them!

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.080
First, representing the You Show School,

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.300
Yuya Sakaki!

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:32.670
Next, representing the Gongenzaka 
Dojo, Noboru Gongenzaka!

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:38.410
And representing the Leo Duel 
School, Shingo Sawatari!

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:40.170
What the heck is that?

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.360
And the last one...

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.940
Uh... I-It's secret?

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:48.360
Well, I guess we'll find out when it starts!

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.860
Hey, where's the principal, anyway?

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:52.040
He said he needed to check something out...

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.240
How dare he?!

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.390
With Yuya here, getting his 
big chance on stage.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:57.620
Darn it...

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.100
And what was it he had to check?

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:02.600
H-How should we know?

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.700
Looks like it's about to start!

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:09.670
Okay, the players have taken their places.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.810
Now, let's start the battle royal!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:19.680
Field Spell Quartet of Quandry, activate!

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.270
I've felt this feeling before, somewhere.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:43.060
Hey...

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:45.770
He said four competitors earlier, right?

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:46.520
Yeah.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:49.850
But clearly, there are only three of us.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.160
What outrageous person would arrive late?

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.420
That would be I!

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:59.860
I am Tsukikage, of the Fuma Clan.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:01.130
Tsukikage?

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.330
Then, the players are all on the stage.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.590
I'm gonna win this duel, no problem!

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.140
Yuya...

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:13.370
I, the man Gongenzaka, will show no mercy.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.210
Prepare yourself.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.000
Sure, bring it on!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.580
I'll show you the ultimate 
entertainment duel!

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:24.200
The duelists meet at the battlefield!

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:28.570
Along with their monsters, they'll kick 
the ground and fly through the sky

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:31.460
to move around the field!

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.750
Witness dueling's greatest evolution.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.260
Action...

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:37.450
Duel!

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:42.510
Let's go! I'll go first!

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:46.740
I summon Performapal Hip Hippo from my hand!

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:54.180
And I set two cards and end my turn!

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.920
Let's go, Hippo.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:03.190
Yuya Sakaki makes the first move!

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:08.010
After ending his turn, 
he's riding his monster around!

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:13.000
Sakaki's special strategy uses Action Cards!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:16.630
I feel like I've seen this before... 
I wonder where it was.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.100
An orange? No, it's something else...

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:24.310
Okay! My turn, next! Draw!

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:28.280
I summon Abyss Actor — Curtain Raiser!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:40.090
Battle... Abyss Actor — Curtain 
Raiser attacks Hip Hippo!

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:45.930
And Curtain Raiser's 
monster effect activates!

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:50.060
When Curtain Raiser is the only 
monster on my side of the field,

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:53.700
its attack points are doubled, 
for damage calculation only.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:55.540
Hippo...

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.210
You found one, huh? Go!

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.920
Action Spell Evasion!

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.120
Rolling Hippo!

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:12.510
Damn.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:16.020
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:19.800
I'm next! Draw!

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.770
I summon Superheavy Samurai 
Flutist from my hand!

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:30.940
I activate Flutist's monster effect!

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:33.680
I tribute it to Special Summon

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:38.050
Superheavy Samurai Big Benkei, 
from my hand, in defense position!

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:47.500
Big Benkei can attack from defense position!

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:48.520
Battle!

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.220
Big Benkei attacks Hip Hippo!

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:01.360
I activate Quick-Play Spell Hippo Carnival!

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:05.410
I Special Summon three Hippo 
Tokens in defense position!

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:12.150
Now, your monsters can 
only attack Hippo Tokens!

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.380
Not bad, Yuya.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.560
I end my turn.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:21.910
Now, the next player—

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:24.030
Remember, all of you!

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:27.510
The last tournament in which we fought.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.230
The Maiami Championship!

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:36.470
The Maiami...

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.880
Champion...

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:38.940
...ship?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.200
The Maiami Championship?

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.550
Oh, I totally forgot about that...

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:48.320
Hmm... Why did we forget?

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.230
Yeah, it really gave me the shivers!

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:55.790
Yeah, because Michy was there! Michy!

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:59.000
That's the main thing... you remembered?

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.450
I... I also remember now...

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.330
the commentary I provided back then!

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.200
Such amazing déjà vu!

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.630
That's right...

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:13.180
During the Maiami Championship's first match,

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:17.380
Yuya Sakaki and I produced one of the 
greatest entertainment duels ever.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:20.030
We had the spectators raving,

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.860
and then I lost...

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.160
I remember, too!

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:29.660
I really have been on this field before.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:31.400
Sora Shiunin...

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:35.170
And he was dueling... Tsukikage?

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:39.030
That was Hikage. My older brother.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.000
I recognize this field, as well.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.700
But if I lost in the first round, 
why was I in the battle royal?

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:50.610
You were given a second chance!

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.710
Oh, yeah...

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.520
Reiji Akaba acknowledged me,

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.690
and brought me back to 
fight the Obelisk Force!

00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.500
The Obelisk Force...

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.890
The elite squadron sent by Leo Akaba, 
Duel Academia's leader,

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.730
who was plotting to invade 
all the dimensions.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:09.000
Leo Akaba... Isn't that Reiji Akaba's father?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.660
Alongside Kurosaki and the others,

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:14.070
we fought against the Obelisk Force.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.040
Kurosaki?

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.980
That's right...

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:20.780
The Maiami Championship's real purpose was

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:25.680
to recruit duelists for a squad, 
the Lancers, to fight Academia,

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:28.620
invaders who used duels as weapons!

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.160
Indeed. That is correct.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:34.630
Well done, Tsukikage.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.130
Continue the duel.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.700
Show no mercy.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.070
Yes, sir.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:42.500
To the field!

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:44.870
It is my turn!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:51.150
Reiji, are we really doing the right thing?

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.470
Will this duel really allow my child...

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:56.810
Allow Layra to smile again?

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.570
Of course.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.290
Yuya Sakaki is the only one who 
can restore Layra's smile.

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.380
But in order to do that...

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:07.460
Yuya must first scale a high wall.

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:15.390
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 1 Twilight Ninja Jogen

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:20.390
and Scale 10 Twilight Ninja Kagen!

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:29.540
I can now summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 9 simultaneously.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.750
Pendulum Summon! Appear!

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:37.790
Twilight Ninja Shingetsu!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.990
And Twilight Ninja Getsuga, the Shogun!

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.760
And I activate Continuous Spell

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:47.000
Illusion Ninjitsu Art of Hazy 
Shuriken from my hand.

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:51.670
Battle! Shingetsu attacks Hippo Token!

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:54.470
Hippo!

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:59.410
Okay, that's mine!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.080
Your Hippo is beaten!

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:05.820
By adding a card to my hand,

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:09.310
I can activate Art of Hazy Shuriken's effect.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:15.290
By sending that card to the graveyard, 
I can deal 300 damage to you.

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:29.670
In that instant, I activate 
Jogen's Pendulum Effect.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:34.550
Once per turn, when a Ninja attacks 
a monster in defense position,

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:37.800
it deals piercing damage, equal to the 
difference between its attack points

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.650
and the opponent's defense points!

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:42.240
The Hippo Token has 0 defense points.

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.520
Shingetsu has 1500 attack points.

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:46.860
In other words, 1500 damage.

00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:53.030
Keep at it, Yuya!

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:55.610
Show no mercy, Tsukikage.

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:58.760
Crush Yuya Sakaki!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:00.240
Reiji...

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.110
If you do this, my child will...

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.210
If that's enough to defeat him,

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:10.910
then Yuya was never a good 
enough duelist, to begin with.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:13.840
Mother,

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.120
I am very sorry for what I said.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.590
But you can give up on Layra smiling.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.980
My turn is not yet over.

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.300
I activate Kagen's Pendulum Effect.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:31.270
It gains the Pendulum Effect of Jogen, 
the other monster in my Pendulum Zone.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:33.390
The same as Jogen?!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:34.870
The piercing effect again?

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:38.610
Battle... Getsuga attacks Hippo Token!

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:42.780
Getsuga has 2000 attack points.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:45.880
That's 2000 points of piercing damage!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.760
But Yuya has 2200 life points.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:50.150
It won't finish the job.

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:52.670
Kagen's second effect activates!

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:56.330
Once per turn, when one of 
my Ninja monsters attacks,

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.900
that monster's attack points increase by 500!

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.030
What?

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:04.740
Oh! If this goes through, 
his life will fall to 0!

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:08.670
Will Yuya be out of the fight already?!

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:51.020
Riding duels,

00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:52.620
D-Wheels,

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:57.290
and the Smile World that 
Edo Phoenix tore in half.

00:23:57.750 --> 00:24:00.600
That's right! To fight Duel Academia,

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:05.820
we headed through the Synchro and Xyz 
Dimensions, to the Fusion Dimension.

00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:09.290
When we did, we were looking for someone...

00:24:10.430 --> 00:24:14.600
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Overflowing Memories.

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:16.860
The fun is only getting started!
